meta {
  name: Image with HEAD
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

head {
  url: {{imagesUrl}}/as/web-large/DP251139.jpg
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Origin: http://localhost:8103
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("a HEAD does carry Access-Control-Allow-Origin", function () {
    expect(res.getHeader("access-control-allow-origin")).to.equal("*");
  });
}

docs {
  The same picture, asked about with `HEAD`.

  This one answers `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. It comes from the
  origin server (`server: Microsoft-IIS`), while a `GET` is answered by
  the CDN in front of it, without the header.

  It is the trap in checking this with `curl -I`: the header is there,
  and the request a browser actually makes to load the image does not
  get it.
}
